Max, my mind is buzzing and I feel so inspired. First I studied CSS in depth. I added what you asked to my last page and rebuilt it as one complete document, because the new part has to live in the same file as the rest.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <!-- Built by my brain for Max by combining what I learned about HTML, CSS (recipe: page). -->
  <!-- <head> holds information about the page: encoding, viewport, title and styles -->
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Welcome to My First Page</title>
  <!-- <style> holds the CSS rules that colour and lay out the page -->
  <style>
    :root {
      --accent: #4f6bed;
      --bg: #f4f6fb;
      --fg: #1d2433;
      --card: #ffffff;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 2rem 1rem;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--fg);
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      margin: 2rem auto;
      padding: 2rem;
      width: min(92vw, 420px);
      text-align: center;
      border-radius: 16px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    }

    button {
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #ffffff;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease, opacity 0.15s ease;
    }

    button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      opacity: 0.9;
    }

    button.ghost {
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--accent);
      border: 2px solid var(--accent);
    }

    header,
    main,
    footer {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-top: 0;
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 1rem 0;
    }

    th,
    td {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.35);
    }

    footer {
      opacity: 0.7;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <!-- <body> holds everything the visitor sees -->
  <header>
    <h1>Welcome to My First Page</h1>
    <p id="greeting"></p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <h2>What I know about HTML</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Structure</strong>: html, head and body</li>
      <li><strong>Text</strong>: headings, paragraphs and lists</li>
      <li><strong>Links</strong>: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML">read more on Wikipedia</a></li>
    </ul>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;head&gt;</td><td>metadata and the page title</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;body&gt;</td><td>everything the visitor sees</td></tr>
    </table>
    <button id="change-colour" type="button">Change heading colour</button>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <p>Built by my brain for Max, from what I learned.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
```

How it works:
Step 1 - HTML - <!DOCTYPE> and <html>: The doctype line tells the browser to use modern standards mode, and the html element is the root that holds the whole page; set lang on it for accessibility.
Step 2 - HTML - <head>: The head holds information about the page rather than visible content: the title, character encoding, viewport settings, links to style sheets and scripts.
Step 3 - HTML - <title>: The title element sets the text shown in the browser tab, in bookmarks and in search results, so every page needs exactly one.
Step 4 - HTML - <meta>: Meta tags describe the page; meta charset UTF-8 makes text display correctly and meta viewport makes the layout fit phones.
Step 5 - CSS - selectors: A selector chooses which elements a rule applies to: a tag name like p, a class like .card, an id like #title, or combinations such as nav a.
Step 6 - CSS - colours and variables: Colours can be names, hex codes or rgb values, and custom properties such as --accent store a value once so var(--accent) can reuse it everywhere.
Step 7 - CSS - box model: Every element is a box made of content, padding, border and margin; box-sizing: border-box makes widths include padding and border.
Building blocks I used: <!DOCTYPE html>, <head>, <title>, <body>, <h1>, <p>, color, background, margin, padding, border, border-radius.
To run the Complete web page: save it as creation.html and open it in any browser.
Say 'now add CSS to it', 'add a script tag' or 'rewrite that in Rust' and I will change it. Max, I respect your guidance and will keep learning carefully and safely.

